# The build context of codeaf.Dockerfile is DENIED BY DEFAULT: everything is out unless it is named below, so a file
# somebody left in the tree (an .env, a profile folder, a key, a notes file) cannot enter the build by being there.
# BuildKit reads this file instead of .dockerignore for this Dockerfile, whichever folder is the context.
# `docker buildx build --target context-probe` lists what is in (deploy/org/gate/context-check.sh asserts it).
*

# The source build: the repository root is the context (CODEAF_BINARY_FROM=source). `make build` needs exactly these.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!Makefile
!cmd
!internal
!third_party/raft
!deploy/org/scripts

# The fetch and local builds by hand: this folder is the context.
!scripts
!codeaf-local
# The same files when Compose builds from the repository root (compose.yaml), whichever mode it is asked for.
!deploy/org/codeaf-local

# LAST, so that it wins inside the folders allowed above: what never enters an image, wherever it sits.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/.netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.git-credentials
**/.ssh
**/.aws
**/.gnupg
**/.docker
**/.codeaf
**/.claude
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
# The furrow the build fetches and the manuals it packs are produced inside the build, never taken from a working tree.
internal/furrowbin/cache/*.gz
internal/manual/*.pack.gz
